<title>SINGAPORE: Wearnes Intl full year net up 4.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Wearnes Intl full year net up 4.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    19.28  vs  18.43</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)			 2.50  vs   2.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   10.00  vs  11.80</p>
<p>    Turnover			     437.07  vs 337.89</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	2.94  vs   2.82</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.41  vs   1.21</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     4.11  vs   2.71</p>
<p>    Profits from associates   (loss) 0.37  vs   0.04 (gain)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			44.21  vs  37.44</p>
<p>    Tax				     13.15  vs  10.67</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (gain) 5.89  vs   4.45 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     (loss) 2.36  vs   nil</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: April 14, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: 2 April 1997</p>
<p>Note - Diversified trading group Wearnes International Ltd said second half results were lower mainly due to reduced contribution from the automotive &amp; equipment division. It reported an extraordinary loss of S$2.4 million mainly due to discontinuation of food equipment activity in Australia and loss in disposing of an associated company in Indonesia. Automotive  </p>
<p>division performance in financial year 1997 would depend on improvement in the economies of Taiwan, Thailand and Singapore. The company said overall 1997 results may be lower. Net profits were before extraordinaries and minorities. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
